# Trivy scanner ignore list for Panakoes.
#
# Format: one rule id (or CVE id) per line. Optional `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` field
# sets a re-evaluation deadline (Trivy ignores the entry past that date so
# the finding resurfaces and we revisit). Path-scoped ignores are written
# as `<rule>:<path>` on one line.
#
# Each entry below MUST have a comment explaining (1) why this is a false
# positive or accepted risk, and (2) when we revisit.
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT paste the literal placeholder string from the
# offending source file into a comment here. Trivy scans this file
# itself for secrets (under a renamed copy named `trivyignores`) and
# will match the same regex against any string in this file. Reference
# the placeholder by description only.

# stripe-secret-token: billing config TEST-mode default placeholder
# (full reasoning lives in services/billing/src/panakoes_billing/config.py
# alongside the validator that enforces the prefix; do not duplicate
# the literal string here).
# Revisit: when billing config moves entirely to AWS Secrets Manager and
# the placeholder default is removed (tracked: SCOPE.md billing hardening).
# exp:2026-08-09
stripe-secret-token:services/billing/src/panakoes_billing/config.py
